# ADR-0042 Slice 5 negative control: `makec`'s return is written as the bare
# leaf `Class` inside a `module Digest` reopen. RBS resolves it lexically to
# `Digest::Class`; rigor-rs's flat return slot keeps only the leaf, and the
# lexical walk sees BOTH `Digest::Class` and top-level `Class` — residual
# ambiguity, so the qualified return path must DECLINE (silent), never guess.
module Digest
  class MakerZzz
    def self.makec: () -> Class
  end
end
